{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["Like grain from the threshing floor — that it is subject to ״כָּל־זָר לֹא־יֹאכַל קֹדֶשׁ״ in the passage of terumah, in ״אֱמֹר אֶל־הַכֹּהֲנִים״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The lemma reads כדגן מן הגורן but the verse itself says כמלא הרמה; the phrase כדגן מן הגורן appears in verse 23 (referring to the Levites' tithe). Rashbam apparently cites verse 23's language while explaining its equivalence to priestly terumah, which is governed by the prohibition of כל זר לא יאכל קדש in Leviticus 22:10 (אמור אל הכהנים)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:50:34.179693868Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}